-- Medical bank audit, 2026-11-25. Fixes what the check of the MDCAT, NUMS, AKU, FSc and Army banks found:
-- 1. About 35 stems leaned on a textbook table or figure the student cannot see ("Using Table 13.1, ..."). Each now
--    gives the data it needs or asks the fact directly; explanations that quoted "the table" are reworded.
-- 2. Raw notation (X_C, k_BT, e^(-t/RC), 10^-7) in about 190 Physics, Chemistry and AKU Maths questions is written as
--    _{...} and ^{...}, which the site shows as subscripts and superscripts (lib/rich.tsx). Genotypes such as A_bb in
--    Biology are left as they are.
-- 3. Questions that repeated another in the same bank (PHY-7284, CHE-1063, CHE-1044, CHE-1183, CHE-1184 and the verbal
--    LR-1122 to 1124) are replaced by new questions on the same chapter; PHY-6073 and CHE-7186 get their own stems.
--    LR-0129's explanation says "practice", not "practise".
-- Every rewrite writes the full new text, taken from the live text on 2026-11-25.
-- 1-3. Rewritten stems, explanations and repeats; raw notation as _{...} / ^{...} markup (lib/rich.tsx).
