font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''15'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>A</text><rect x=''107.0'' y=''122.0'' width=''74'' height=''74'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''129.2'' cy=''181.2'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''158.8'' cy=''181.2'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''129.2'' cy=''136.8'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''158.8'' cy=''136.8'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''144.0'' y=''212.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''15'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>B</text><rect x=''193.0'' y=''122.0'' width=''74'' height=''74'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''207.8'' cy=''173.8'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''252.2'' cy=''173.8'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''207.8'' cy=''144.2'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''252.2'' cy=''144.2'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''230.0'' y=''212.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''15'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>C</text><rect x=''279.0'' y=''122.0'' width=''74'' height=''74'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''293.8'' cy=''173.8'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><circle cx=''338.2'' cy=''144.2'' r=''5.0'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''316.0'' y=''212.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''15'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>D</text></svg>', '["Figure A", "Figure B", "Figure C", "Figure D"]', 2, 'Unfold one step at a time, starting with the last fold. Each time, every hole is copied as a mirror image across that fold line. The punch goes through 4 layers, so the open sheet has 4 holes.', '{"0": "This shows only the hole in the top layer, but the punch goes through four layers.", "1": "Four holes is right, but each is a quarter-turn out of place: they should be nearer the left and right edges than the top and bottom.", "3": "Two straight folds give a hole in each of the four quarters, not just two."}', 1),
  ('LR-1209', 'Logical Reasoning', 'Patterns and sequences', 'Cubes and dice', 'easy', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The net shown is folded to make a cube. Which face is opposite the face marked A?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''248'' height=''196'' viewBox=''0 0 248 196''><rect x=''20'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''46.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>A</text><rect x=''72'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>B</text><rect x=''124'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''150.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>C</text><rect x=''176'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''202.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>D</text><rect x=''72'' y=''20'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''47.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>E</text><rect x=''72'' y=''124'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''151.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>F</text></svg>', '["B", "E", "C", "D"]', 2, 'In a straight row of faces, two faces with exactly one face between them end up opposite each other. A and C have B between them, so C is opposite A.', '{"0": "B is next to A in the net, so they share an edge on the cube.", "1": "E folds up to become the top, which touches A along an edge.", "3": "D folds round to meet A, so they share an edge. In a row of four, the first and fourth faces are neighbours."}', 1),
  ('LR-1210', 'Logical Reasoning', 'Patterns and sequences', 'Cubes and dice', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The net shown is folded to make a cube. Which face is opposite the face marked P?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''248'' height=''196'' viewBox=''0 0 248 196''><rect x=''20'' y=''20'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''46.0'' y=''47.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>P</text><rect x=''20'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''46.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>Q</text><rect x=''72'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>R</text><rect x=''124'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''150.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>S</text><rect x=''176'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''202.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>T</text><rect x=''176'' y=''124'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''202.0'' y=''151.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>U</text></svg>', '["Q", "U", "R", "T"]', 1, 'Q, R, S and T wrap round to make the four sides of the cube. P, joined above Q, folds over to make the top, and U, joined below T, folds under to make the bottom. Top and bottom are opposite, so U is opposite P.', '{"0": "Q is joined to P in the net, so they are neighbours on the cube.", "2": "R folds up to meet P along an edge, so they are neighbours.", "3": "T is opposite R, two faces further along the row. T folds up beside P, so they share an edge."}', 1)
) AS s
JOIN users u ON u.email = 'hozaiphaa@gmail.com';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO questions
  (id, subject, chapter, topic, difficulty, source, stem, figure, options, answer, why, wrong, mdcat, stage, free, checks, writer_id, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT s.column1, s.column2, s.column3, s.column4, s.column5, s.column6, s.column7, s.column8, s.column9, s.column10, s.column11, s.column12, s.column13,
  'live', 0, '[]', u.id, unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
FROM (VALUES
  ('LR-1211', 'Logical Reasoning', 'Patterns and sequences', 'Cubes and dice', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'The net shown is folded to make a cube. Which face is opposite the face marked 1?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''196'' height=''248'' viewBox=''0 0 196 248''><rect x=''72'' y=''20'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''47.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>1</text><rect x=''72'' y=''72'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''99.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>2</text><rect x=''20'' y=''124'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''46.0'' y=''151.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>3</text><rect x=''72'' y=''124'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''151.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>4</text><rect x=''124'' y=''124'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''150.0'' y=''151.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>5</text><rect x=''72'' y=''176'' width=''52'' height=''52'' fill=''none'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2''/><text x=''98.0'' y=''203.0'' font-family=''Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'' font-size=''22'' text-anchor=''middle'' dominant-baseline=''middle'' fill=''#000'' font-weight=''bold''>6</text></svg>', '["4", "2", "3", "6"]', 0, 'In the column 1, 2, 4, 6, two faces with exactly one face between them end up opposite. 1 and 4 have 2 between them, so 4 is opposite 1. (2 is opposite 6, and 3 is opposite 5.)', '{"1": "2 is joined to 1 in the net, so they are neighbours on the cube.", "2": "3 folds up to the side and meets 1 along an edge.", "3": "1 and 6 lie in the same column, but there are three faces between them, so they end up as neighbours."}', 1),
  ('LR-1212', 'Logical Reasoning', 'Patterns and sequences', 'Cubes and dice', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'A cube is painted on all six faces and then cut into 27 equal small cubes, as shown. How many of the small cubes have exactly two painted faces?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''210'' height=''236'' viewBox=''0 0 210 236''><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''20.0'' x2=''20.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''20.0'' x2=''190.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''190.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''216.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''20.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''216.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''133.3'' y1=''36.4'' x2=''48.3'' y2=''85.4'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''76.7'' y1=''36.4'' x2=''161.7'' y2=''85.4'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''161.7'' y1=''183.6'' x2=''161.7'' y2=''85.4'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''134.5'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''183.6'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''48.3'' y1=''183.6'' x2=''48.3'' y2=''85.4'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''134.5'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''183.6'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''161.7'' y1=''52.7'' x2=''76.7'' y2=''101.8'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''48.3'' y1=''52.7'' x2=''133.3'' y2=''101.8'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''133.3'' y1=''199.9'' x2=''133.3'' y2=''101.8'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''101.8'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''150.9'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''76.7'' y1=''199.9'' x2=''76.7'' y2=''101.8'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''101.8'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''150.9'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''216.3'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''216.3'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/></svg>', '["8", "6", "1", "12"]', 3, 'A small cube has two painted faces when it lies along an edge of the big cube but not at a corner. A cube has 12 edges, and with 3 small cubes along each edge, 1 on each edge is not a corner. So 12 × 1 = 12.', '{"0": "8 is the number of corner cubes, which have three painted faces.", "1": "6 is the number of cubes in the middle of a face, which have one painted face.", "2": "1 is the single cube in the very centre, which has no paint at all."}', 1),
  ('LR-1213', 'Logical Reasoning', 'Patterns and sequences', 'Cubes and dice', 'hard', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'A cube is painted on all six faces and then cut into 64 equal small cubes, as shown. How many of the small cubes have no paint on them?', '<svg xmlns=''http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'' width=''210'' height=''236'' viewBox=''0 0 210 236''><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''20.0'' x2=''20.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''20.0'' x2=''190.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''190.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''216.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''20.0'' y2=''69.1'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''167.2'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''216.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''126.3'' y1=''32.3'' x2=''41.3'' y2=''81.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''83.8'' y1=''32.3'' x2=''168.8'' y2=''81.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''168.8'' y1=''179.5'' x2=''168.8'' y2=''81.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''142.7'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''191.8'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''41.3'' y1=''179.5'' x2=''41.3'' y2=''81.3'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''142.7'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''191.8'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''147.5'' y1=''44.5'' x2=''62.5'' y2=''93.6'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''62.5'' y1=''44.5'' x2=''147.5'' y2=''93.6'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''147.5'' y1=''191.8'' x2=''147.5'' y2=''93.6'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''118.2'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''167.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''62.5'' y1=''191.8'' x2=''62.5'' y2=''93.6'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''118.2'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''167.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''168.8'' y1=''56.8'' x2=''83.8'' y2=''105.9'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''41.3'' y1=''56.8'' x2=''126.3'' y2=''105.9'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''126.3'' y1=''204.0'' x2=''126.3'' y2=''105.9'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''93.6'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''142.7'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''83.8'' y1=''204.0'' x2=''83.8'' y2=''105.9'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''93.6'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''142.7'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''1.3'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''216.3'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''190.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''105.0'' y1=''216.3'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/><line x1=''20.0'' y1=''69.1'' x2=''105.0'' y2=''118.2'' stroke=''#000'' stroke-width=''2.2'' stroke-linecap=''round''/></svg>', '["24", "16", "8", "0"]', 2, 'The unpainted cubes are the ones hidden inside, not touching any face. Removing the outer layer from a 4 × 4 × 4 cube leaves a 2 × 2 × 2 block, which is 8 small cubes.', '{"0": "24 is the number with exactly one painted face (4 on each of the 6 faces). It is also the number with exactly two.", "1": "16 is the number of small cubes showing on one face of the big cube.", "3": "A 4 × 4 × 4 cube has an inner block of cubes that the paint never reaches."}', 1)
) AS s
JOIN users u ON u.email = 'hozaiphaa@gmail.com';

